---
title: Koftesi
description: Grilled chicken with yoghurt, hot pepper, and garlic
course: Main
locale: en_GB
prep time: 30m
cook time: 10m
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Turkish
tags:
- main-course
- savoury
- meat
- kebabs
- turkish
---

Place @Aleppo pepper{1%tbsp} in a small bowl and add @warm water{1%tbsp}. Let stand for about ~{5%minutes} until a thick paste forms.

Place the pepper paste in a large non-reactive bowl. Add the @greek yoghurt{235%ml}, @olive oil{3%tbsp}, @red wine vinegar{2%tbsp}, @tomato purée{2%tbsp}, @coarse salt{1.5%tsp} and @black pepper{1%tsp}(freshly ground). Whisk to mix. Stir in the @garlic{6%cloves}(peeled and crushed) and @lemon{1}(thinly sliced and seeds removed).

Add the @chicken thighs or breast, skinless and boneless{700%g}(cut into 1×1×½ inch pieces) to the marinade and stir to coat evenly. Let the chicken marinate in the refrigerator, covered, for at least 1 hour or as long as ~{4%hours}. The longer the chicken marinates, the richer the flavour will be.

Thread the chicken through the thin side onto skewers so that the flat side of the chicken will be exposed to the fire.

When ready to cook sprinkle each chicken kebab on both sides with @coarse salt{}, @black pepper{}, and the remaining @Aleppo pepper{1%tbsp}. Grill until nicely browned and cooked through, 2 to ~{4%minutes} per side.